# CTRLO-AT-KEYS: one key at a time under Ctrl-O while the @ list is up
# (AT-HEIGHT's ctrlo-probe, extended). Each step opens Ctrl-O over the list,
# sends one key, closes it again, and snaps the composer's plane. fx's list
# is not eligible under the transcript (filePickerEligible,
# input_completion_runtime.zig:775-786@481104fd), and the bytes the
# transcript does not bind reach the composer (app_input_runtime.zig:
# 872-893): Tab chooses nothing (input_completion_runtime.zig:946-956), a
# letter is typed, C-k kills to the line's end, C-j is a new line. Down and
# Escape are the transcript's (input_full_transcript_runtime.zig:156-197).
# C-e C-u empties the line before a step that needs its own draft, so no
# step's result carries into the next.
fx: env FX_AUTO_UPGRADE=0
work p5-input-at-height-ws
wait 4
type @f-
wait 1.5
snap open
key C-o
wait 0.8
key Tab
wait 0.4
key C-o
wait 0.8
snap tab
key C-o
wait 0.8
key Down
wait 0.4
key C-o
wait 0.8
snap down
key C-o
wait 0.8
key Escape
wait 0.8
snap esc
key C-o
wait 0.8
type z
wait 0.4
key C-o
wait 1
snap letter
key C-e C-u
wait 0.4
type  tail
key Home
wait 0.3
type @f-
wait 1.5
snap tail-open
key C-o
wait 0.8
key C-k
wait 0.4
key C-o
wait 0.8
snap ck
key C-e C-u
wait 0.4
type @f-
wait 1.5
key C-o
wait 0.8
key C-j
wait 0.4
key C-o
wait 0.8
snap cj
